{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/625108-running-danzig-as-an-antagonist","id":625108,"title":"Running Danzig as an Antagonist","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-12T22:28:41-07:00","id":625108,"title":"Running Danzig as an Antagonist","content":"I'm transitioning my campaign from NYC to Tokyo in preparation for Hurt Locker. I plan to use Danzig as a reoccurring contact/ally/antagonist for the group, someone they can speak with, even make deals with... while still presenting the dangers of a powerful Exile who wants them to accept reintegration with the G-M.<br /> <br /> In that wildly optimistic game all GMs/storytellers envision, I can see Danzig as a subtle, ever present threat: the good cop to the bad cop angels, Mr. Smith in the restaurant with Cypher (matrix).<br /> <br /> More realistically, Danzig's schtick is a very hard sell. He's offering total destruction of a character, not much in a way of benefit, and he won't use his otherwise considerable power to force them if they simply smile and say, &quot;You want us to surrender our free will to an alien AI? You won't use violence or attack us? Okay, good talk.&quot;<br /> <br /> Has anyone used Danzig in a chronicle? Any tips on presenting him in a way that the players won't brush him off with nary a backward glance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 08-13-2015, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T23:03:14-07:00","id":625143,"title":"","content":"So I'ma presume you mean <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ksitigarbha\" target=\"_blank\">this guy</a> and not <a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/78/Danzig_at_Sweden_Rock.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this guy</a>.<br /> <br /> If you have Integrators in the ring, or demons with Integrator sympathies, Dizang is where you introduce a shoulder to lean on, a point of tension with other ringmates, and a potential road to Heaven. Dizang will probably default to making arguments in support of recycling, but an Integrator determined to rejoin with the Machine on his own terms (in other words, an Integrator who has thought this thing through any) could potentially argue him into a position where he might consider the virtues of alternate returns. And should Dizang be convinced to help an Integrator on that way back to God, he may be an invaluable source of advice for ideas, useful contacts or whatever plot MacGuffins you might cook up to help make integration into the Machine as a loyalist demon rather than a recycled angel a practical goal to achieve.<br /> <br /> If you don't have Integrators, use Dizang to come at the horror of the God-Machine from the other side: the creeping suspicion that, as odious as this master system might be, it might actually still be better than the alternative. Dizang is benevolent. He wants to help. And he knows the good things the God-Machine does. He knows how many lives a project hidden in the Sea of Trees has taken \u2014 and he knows how many more lives might have been preserved by transmitting that project's output elsewhere, to stop earthquakes and stabilize hurricanes. He knows what would happen if the God-Machine's safeguards against Shadow Verges and temporal distortions weren't there to keep the human world separate from that of monsters and impossibilities. He knows how vastly intricate the God-Machine's stability calculations are, and how beyond any individual, even Unchained, it would be to match its foresight. He knows that if you were to tear out all the cables connecting humanity to the God-Machine, it wouldn't just be the God-Machine that died from the shock.<br /> <br /> He believes in sacrifice. He believes that power confers responsibility. And he honestly thinks that it will be better for everyone, in the long term, if you give up your life and everything you are to become a piece of the God that, if it worked properly, could save the world.<br /> <br /> What would you do if somebody asked you to be Christ? Think of how awful that would be, to have that choice in front of you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T14:10:12-07:00","id":625892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/625108-running-danzig-as-an-antagonist?p=625143#post625143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'ma presume you mean <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ksitigarbha\" target=\"_blank\">this guy</a> and not <a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/78/Danzig_at_Sweden_Rock.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this guy</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather hope not, Danzig would be hilarious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T16:19:36-07:00","id":626031,"title":"","content":"yea I thought of Glenn Danzig and was all &quot;Woah, way to be harsh on the players!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T19:53:42-07:00","id":626181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/625108-running-danzig-as-an-antagonist?p=625892#post625892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I rather hope not, Danzig would be hilarious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmmm... fighting Demons with the power of ROCK<br /> <br /> Loserman, that is one of the... creepiest and most helpful pieces of advice I've received on this forum. I'll be printing it out for reference when Danzig shows up in my campaign. While I've got you here, there are some questions that I know my players will ask. Any idea how Danzig might handle these questions:<br /> <br /> 1. &quot;I Fell because I didn't want to murder 30 people, why would I go back to being a tool of murder?&quot; - the ring's destroyer Fell when he wouldn't collapse an occupied church to fuel an Infrastructure. <br /> <br /> 2. &quot;The G-m has severe malfunctions. Why subject ourselves to that if we're not even sure if they can be fixed?&quot; The Integrator. So far in may campaign has empahsized the idea that if the G-m isn't utter amoral then it is at least missing a few screws loose<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T20:37:07-07:00","id":626243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/625108-running-danzig-as-an-antagonist?p=626181#post626181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. &quot;I Fell because I didn't want to murder 30 people, why would I go back to being a tool of murder?&quot; - the ring's destroyer Fell when he wouldn't collapse an occupied church to fuel an Infrastructure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did the destroyer know what purpose it was that he was to serve by collapsing that church? What did the infrastructure do, and what happened in its absence? How far do the rippling repercussions go? Dizang might ask that demon to return to that project he disrupted, and investigate, and find out what events it spiralled into when he Fell.<br /> <br /> (Now, keep in mind Dizang is, while honest and acting in good faith, still a wholly biased party in this matter. Maybe the project was designed for some protective end over a wide swath of the population. Maybe it was wholly parasitic and only really existed to invoke more numerous and more powerful angels, or to store up Essence for future exploitation. Ideally, it might be something in the middle, more complicated and subjective to argue. Maybe killing 30 innocent people was necessary to kill 30 vampires. Was that worth doing? How much harm would those vampires go on to do, and even if you saved more lives than you lost in the long run, does that justify the mass murder of innocents? Did even all of the vampires deserve to be re-killed?)<br /> <br /> Dizang would probably be somewhat melancholy that the murder of innocents might be necessary for some good ends, but that ties back to sacrifice. You're not asked to enjoy your work, or to be happy that 30 innocents died. But if their loss was important and you are the one in the position to do it, would you turn your back because it's uncomfortable work?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/625108-running-danzig-as-an-antagonist?p=626181#post626181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. &quot;The G-m has severe malfunctions. Why subject ourselves to that if we're not even sure if they can be fixed?&quot; The Integrator. So far in may campaign has empahsized the idea that if the G-m isn't utter amoral then it is at least missing a few screws loose</div> </div> </div> </div>Integrator's got a very strong point there, one that Dizang might find it more difficult to argue against. It might even be possible to sway Dizang on this subject if you keep up diligent contact with him and events go the right way. Can an Exile Fall, or undergo some similar process? But that's not to say he wouldn't have any counterpoints. Is it not possible that the Fall itself, the bleeding away of angels to worldly attachments and desires, might be at the root of the God-Machine's malfunctions?<br /> <br /> When you Fell, Integrator, in that moment, you went from being of one substance with God, in holy union, to being alone in the world of flesh. Do you remember the difficulties you had adjusting? The distortions cast by your Fall, the disorientation of losing your Influence, the ragged edges of your Primum at the extremes of your demonic form, where you tore your existence free from the God-Machine?<br /> <br /> Do you think the God-Machine didn't carry some scars from that moment, too?<br /> <br /> Even now, as your Primum expands and you expand the divide between you and God, your demonic body itself mutates and changes. It carries the mark of the impact of everything that began in that moment. You are not the same as you once were.<br /> <br /> Neither is the God you are walking away from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}